 Sustainability, Italy doesn\'t recognise the professional qualifications such as RNCP titles.\n*In some cases, a three-year degree with three years minimum of professional experience after graduation can be accepted. Candidates with an Indian Bachelor degree are eligible for the One-year MSc if they have more than 3 years of work experience after graduation and for the Two-year MSc if they have less than 3 years of work experience.\n\nRequire​ments - MSc (one-year)*: Eligible to apply: Students who hold a four-year university degree or equivalent (240 ECTS credits or RNCP 7) plus at least two months minimum of professional experience (or internship). - For the MSc Financial Markets and Investments, MSc Strategic Management and Consulting and MSc Corporate Financial Management, six months minimum of professional experience. - For the MSc Product Management & UX Design, MSc Entrepreneurship & Design for Sustainability, Italy doesn’t recognise the professional qualifications such as RNCP titles. *In some cases, a three-year degree with three years minimum of professional experience after graduation can be accepted. Candidates with an Indian Bachelor degree are eligible for the One-year MSc if they have more than 3 years of work experience after graduation and for the Two-year MSc if they have less than 3 years of work experience. Require​ments - MSc (one-year)*: Eligible to apply: Students who hold a four-year university degree or equivalent (240 ECTS credits or RNCP 7) plus at least two months minimum of professional experience (or internship). - For the MSc Financial Markets and Investments, MSc Strategic Management and Consulting and MSc Corporate Financial Management, six months minimum of professional experience. - For the MSc Product Management & UX Design, MSc Entrepreneurship & Design for Sustainability, Italy doesn’t recognise the professional qualifications such as RNCP titles. *In some cases, a three-year degree with three years minimum of professional experience after graduation can be accepted. Candidates with an Indian Bachelor degree are eligible for the One-year MSc if they have more than 3 years of work experience after graduation and for the Two-year MSc if they have less than 3 years of work experience.\n\nTOEFL IBT(71), TOEFL ITP(530), IELTS(6), TOEIC(810), Duolingo(105), Cambridge English Qualification®(165), ICIMS (61, on demand).','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:49','2026-07-13 23:24:35',NULL);
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `public_id`, `university_id`, `name`, `degree_level`, `duration_months`, `language`, `description`, `eligibility_criteria`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES (1148,'01KWJDMF1NH5N3RXYPR3DKYQ6G',73,'MSc Sustainable Finance & Fintech','masters',24,'English','Language requirement: TOEFL IBT(71), TOEFL ITP(530), IELTS(6), TOEIC(810), Duolingo(105), Cambridge English Qualification®(165), ICIMS(61, on demand).\n\nToolkit source: non_exclusive / France Spain / row 384.','REQUIREMENTS / DOCUMENTS:\nRequirements - Two-Year​ MSc:\nEligible to apply: students who hold a three-year university degree or equivalent.\nAnd students will be required to reach the necessary level for the MSc before moving to year two.\n Require​ments - MSc (one-year):\nEligible to apply: students who hold a four-year university degree or equivalent + two months minimum of professional experience (for the MSc Financial Markets and Investments, this requirement is: a four-year degree + six months minimum of professional experience),\nStudents with the equivalent of a three-year degree in France, as well as a minimum of three years of professional experience.*\n\nRequirements - Two-Year​ MSc: Eligible to apply: students who hold a three-year university degree or equivalent. And students will be required to reach the necessary level for the MSc before moving to year two. Require​ments - MSc (one-year): Eligible to apply: students who hold a four-year university degree or equivalent + two months minimum of professional experience (for the MSc Financial Markets and Investments, this requirement is: a four-year degree + six months minimum of professional experience), Students with the equivalent of a three-year degree in France, as well as a minimum of three years of professional experience.*\n\nTOEFL IBT(71), TOEFL ITP(530), IELTS(6), TOEIC(810), Duolingo(105), Cambridge English Qualification®(165), ICIMS(61, on demand).','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:49','2026-07-13 23:24:35',NULL);
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `public_id`, `university_id`, `name`, `degree_level`, `duration_months`, `language`, `description`, `eligibility_criteria`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES (1149,'01KWJDMF1PY47592PS6745EVS8',73,'Global MBA | International Triple degree','masters',24,'English','Language requirement: OEFL IBT: Generally around 71 or higher and IELTS Generally around 6.0. , Duolingo English Test: Generally 105 or higher.\n\nToolkit source: non_exclusive / France Spain / row 385.','REQUIREMENTS / DOCUMENTS:\nApplication form\n$50 application fee (waived)\nCurrent résumé\nTwo letters of recommendation from educational and professional references\nOfficial transcripts showing all college work attempted: undergraduate, graduate, and professional. (A translated copy of academic records (transcripts) is required for applicants who attended or completed their bachelor\'s and/or master\'s degree outside of the United States\nCopy of Bachelor\'s Degree Diploma\nOnline interview\nOPTIONAL: An official GMAT or GRE score report.\n400-word essay--statement of purpose - Please keep in mind the following questions when writing your statement:\nWhy do you want to pursue the Global MBA-Triple Master degree?\nHow do you think the triple degree program will enhance your academic and/or professional background?\nWhat makes you an ideal candidate?                                                                                                                                                                          International Applicants:\n- Must also provide an affidavit of support showing sufficient funds to finance their course of study and living expenses.\n- A translated copy of academic records (transcripts) is required for applicants who attended or completed their bachelor\'s and/or master\'s degree outside of the United States. Students can request transcript evaluation through WES, ECE, or SpanTran.\n- Applicants from China or Vietnam must submit APSCertificate\n- When asked to enter a CEEB code, if your academic institution is unlisted, please enter 000004 for an unlisted international school.\n\nApplication form $50 application fee (waived) Current résumé Two letters of recommendation from educational and professional references Official transcripts showing all college work attempted: undergraduate, graduate, and professional. (A translated copy of academic records (transcripts) is required for applicants who attended or completed their bachelor’s and/or master’s degree outside of the United States Copy of Bachelor’s Degree Diploma Online interview OPTIONAL: An official GMAT or GRE score report. 400-word essay--statement of purpose - Please keep in mind the following questions when writing your statement: Why do you want to pursue the Global MBA-Triple Master degree? How do you think the triple degree program will enhance your academic and/or professional background? What makes you an ideal candidate? International Applicants: - Must also provide an affidavit of support showing sufficient funds to finance their course of study and living expenses. - A translated copy of academic records (transcripts) is required for applicants who attended or completed their bachelor’s and/or master’s degree outside of the United States. Students can request transcript evaluation through WES, ECE, or SpanTran. - Applicants from China or Vietnam must submit APSCertificate - When asked to enter a CEEB code, if your academic institution is unlisted, please enter 000004 for an unlisted international school.\n\nOEFL IBT: Generally around 71 or higher and IELTS Generally around 6.0. , Duolingo English Test: Generally 105 or higher.','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:49','2026-07-13 23:24:35',NULL);
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `public_id`, `university_id`, `name`, `degree_level`, `duration_months`, `language`, `description`, `eligibility_criteria`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES (1150,'01KWJDMF1Q7QHJ53YXPC3ZR4FG',74,'Bachelor of Science in Computer Science','bachelors',36,'English','Language requirement: TOEFL (minimum score 80 IBT) // TOEIC (minimum score 800) // IELTS (minimum score 6.0)\n\nToolkit source: non_exclusive / France Spain / row 388.','REQUIREMENTS / DOCUMENTS:\nThe program is open to applicants holding a high school diploma, or who are in their first year of a bachelor\'s program (or equivalent) in Computer Science or related fields. Applicants need to have a strong background in mathematics and general sciences. Documents Required:- CV, Passport, Scan Copy of certified High School Certificate, 2 Letter of Recommendation and Statement of Purpose, Application fee: €60 / Payable upon submitting application\n\nThe program is open to applicants holding a high school diploma, or who are in their first year of a bachelor’s program (or equivalent) in Computer Science or related fields. Applicants need to have a strong background in mathematics and general sciences. Documents Required:- CV, Passport, Scan Copy of certified High School Certificate, 2 Letter of Recommendation and Statement of Purpose, Application fee: €60 / Payable upon submitting application\n\nTOEFL (minimum score 80 IBT) // TOEIC (minimum score 800) // IELTS (minimum score 6.0)','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:49','2026-07-13 23:24:35',NULL);
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `public_id`, `university_id`, `name`, `degree_level`, `duration_months`, `language`, `description`, `eligibility_criteria`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES (1151,'01KWJDMF1RRBZM5X4PZCPJFMNG',74,'MSC Computer Science','masters',18,'English','Language requirement: TOEFL (minimum score 80 IBT) // TOEIC (minimum score 800) // IELTS (minimum score 6.0)\n\nToolkit source: non_exclusive / France Spain / row 389.','REQUIREMENTS / DOCUMENTS:\nThe program is open to candidates holding a 4-year Bachelor\'s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering or related fields. Students with a 3-year Bachelor\'s degree with related work experience can also apply!   Documents Required:-  CV, Passport, Scan Copy of certified High School Certificate, 2 Letter of Recommendation and Statement of Purpose, Application fee: €60 / Payable upon submitting application\n\nThe program is open to candidates holding a 4-year Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering or related fields. Students with a 3-year Bachelor’s degree with related work experience can also apply! Documents Required:- CV, Passport, Scan Copy of certified High School Certificate, 2 Letter of Recommendation and Statement of Purpose, Application fee: €60 / Payable upon submitting application\n\nTOEFL (minimum score 80 IBT) // TOEIC (minimum score 800) // IELTS (minimum score 6.0)','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:49','2026-07-13 23:24:35',NULL);
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `public_id`, `university_id`, `name`, `degree_level`, `duration_months`, `language`, `description`, `eligibility_criteria`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES (1152,'01KWJDMF1RRBZM5X4PZCPJFMNK',74,'MSC Artifcial Intelligence Systems','masters',24,'English','Toolkit source: non_exclusive / France Spain / row 390.','REQUIREMENTS / DOCUMENTS:\nThe program is open to applicants holding a 4-year bachelor\'s degree (or equivalent) in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering or related fields. There are no age restrictions. Students can join this program immediately after receiving their Bachelor degree or later in their careers. Applicants need to have a strong background in mathematics and general sciences.  Documents Required:-  CV, Passport, Scan Copy of certified High School Certificate, 2 Letter of Recommendation and Statement of Purpose, Application fee: €60 / Payable upon submitting application\nBachlelor - RNCP 6\n\nThe program is open to applicants holding a 4-year bachelor’s degree (or equivalent) in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering or related fields. There are no age restrictions. Students can join this program immediately after receiving their Bachelor degree or later in their careers. Applicants need to have a strong background in mathematics and general sciences. Documents Required:- CV, Passport, Scan Copy of certified High School Certificate, 2 Letter of Recommendation and Statement of Purpose, Application fee: €60 / Payable upon submitting application\n\nTOEFL (minimum score 80 IBT) // TOEIC (minimum score 800) // IELTS (minimum score 6.0)','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:49','2026-07-13 23:24:35',NULL);
