cate or Provisional Certificate must be awarded by the University and not the College. Transcript of records The Transcript of Records may be awarded by the College.','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:50','2026-07-13 23:24:38',NULL);
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `public_id`, `university_id`, `name`, `degree_level`, `duration_months`, `language`, `description`, `eligibility_criteria`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES (1967,'01KWJDMFK5EQ7G4WBEAYHP79D9',124,'Commercial Aviation Management (CAM)','bachelors',36,'English','Toolkit source: non_exclusive / Estonia / row 64.','ELIGIBILITY:\nThe Applicants must present proof of their English language skills at level B2 or above. The following tests and scores are accepted:\n\nresult of the Estonian national examination in English corresponding at least to level B2;\nat least 75 points scored in the Estonian national examination in English taken before 2014;\nTOEFL iBT score at least 75;\nIELTS Academic (International English Language Testing Service) score at least 5.5 in each band;\nCambridge tests B2 First (FCE), C1 Advanced (CAE) and C2 Proficiency (CPE), score at least 169;\nPearson Test of English (PTE) Academic and Academic online, score at least 59;\nAviation English proficiency at least at level 4 (ICAO)\n\nREQUIREMENTS / DOCUMENTS:\nonline application;\na copy of an identity document (passport or ID card);\na document certifying secondary education and a transcript of results (please see country-specific requirements);\ndocument certifying English language proficiency of at least B2 level;\nconfirmation/receipt of application fee (€50), the invoice will be sent to you after you have submitted your application.\n\nThe Applicants must present proof of their English language skills at level B2 or above. The following tests and scores are accepted: result of the Estonian national examination in English corresponding at least to level B2; at least 75 points scored in the Estonian national examination in English taken before 2014; TOEFL iBT score at least 75; IELTS Academic (International English Language Testing Service) score at least 5.5 in each band; Cambridge tests B2 First (FCE), C1 Advanced (CAE) and C2 Proficiency (CPE), score at least 169; Pearson Test of English (PTE) Academic and Academic online, score at least 59; Aviation English proficiency at least at level 4 (ICAO)\n\nonline application; a copy of an identity document (passport or ID card); a document certifying secondary education and a transcript of results (please see country-specific requirements); document certifying English language proficiency of at least B2 level; confirmation/receipt of application fee (€50), the invoice will be sent to you after you have submitted your application.','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:50','2026-07-13 23:24:38',NULL);
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `public_id`, `university_id`, `name`, `degree_level`, `duration_months`, `language`, `description`, `eligibility_criteria`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES (1968,'01KWJDMFK73M64NVC888DF7W7W',125,'International Business Administration - Marketing & Communication','bachelors',36,'English','Toolkit source: non_exclusive / Estonia / row 67.','ELIGIBILITY:\nRequirements for internationally recognised language tests:    \n\nTOEFL iBT score 87 \nPlease note that the TOEFL test result is valid 2 years!\nIELTS Academic (International English Language Testing Service) 5.5 with or above in each individual component.\nPlease note that the IELTS test result is valid 2 years!\nCambridge test FCE (CAE; CPE are suitable as well)\nDuolingo language test score 100 points\n\nREQUIREMENTS / DOCUMENTS:\nSubmits online application in DreamApply;\nHolds a higher secondary education degree or an equivalent qualification;\nCheck country-specific requirements to ensure the qualification you have is considered suitable for applying to bachelor-level studies\nHolds sufficient proficiency in English (B2);\nA list of accepted internationally recognised language tests is provided below; \nDemonstrates their motivation, ambition and argumentation skills in a catchy application;\nCompletes the admission interview at EBS.\n\nRequirements for internationally recognised language tests: TOEFL iBT score 87 Please note that the TOEFL test result is valid 2 years! IELTS Academic (International English Language Testing Service) 5.5 with or above in each individual component. Please note that the IELTS test result is valid 2 years! Cambridge test FCE (CAE; CPE are suitable as well) Duolingo language test score 100 points\n\nSubmits online application in DreamApply; Holds a higher secondary education degree or an equivalent qualification; Check country-specific requirements to ensure the qualification you have is considered suitable for applying to bachelor-level studies Holds sufficient proficiency in English (B2); A list of accepted internationally recognised language tests is provided below; Demonstrates their motivation, ambition and argumentation skills in a catchy application; Completes the admission interview at EBS.','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:50','2026-07-13 23:24:38',NULL);
