or\'s Degree from a recognized university and must demonstrate proficiency in English. (Source: Master of Business Administration (MBA) Program) MSc in Applied Psychology: Prospective students should have a bachelor\'s degree of a minimum of three years in any discipline with at least 50% aggregate marks from a recognized university. (Source: Master of Science in Applied Psychology) MSc in Medical Biotechnology: Eligibility criteria require students to hold a bachelor\'s degree in any Life Science subject from a recognized university with at least 50% aggregate marks in their undergraduate degree. (Source: Msc in Medical Biotechnology) MSc in Information Science: Candidates should be a graduate with a BSc(IT)/BSc(ISM)/BCA/BSc (Computer Science)/B.Sc./BBA (IT)/B. Tech/B.E from a recognized University or any other graduate with a minimum of three years of experience in the field of IT. (Source: MSc Information Systems)\n\n1. A bachelor’s degree in Food & Nutrition Science, Life Sciences or allied areas from a recognised university Have passed the examinations with at least 50% marks in aggregate 2. Minimum 60% in English in the qualifying exam. If not met, applicants must clear the Manipal Enablers English Competency Test and/or complete a 6-week Bridge Program with a minimum 60% pass grade. If the medium of instruction was not English, submit IELTS/TOEFL with an overall score of 6','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:50','2026-07-13 23:24:41',NULL);
