le to fresh graduates, working executives, and self-employed professionals. 2. Minimum 60% in English in the qualifying exam. If not met, applicants must clear the Manipal Enablers English Competency Test and/or complete a 6-week Bridge Program with a minimum 60% pass grade. If the medium of instruction was not English, submit IELTS/TOEFL with an overall score of 6.','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:50','2026-07-13 23:24:41',NULL);
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `public_id`, `university_id`, `name`, `degree_level`, `duration_months`, `language`, `description`, `eligibility_criteria`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES (2530,'01KWJDMG0Q6WDB86WWF8AVRERD',145,'MSc - Food Science and Safety','bachelors',24,'English','Toolkit source: non_exclusive / UAE / row 69.','REQUIREMENTS / DOCUMENTS:\n1. BSc in Food and Nutrition Sciences, Allied Sciences (such as Medical, Agriculture, BHMS, BAMS), Life Sciences (including Botany, Zoology, Biotechnology, Microbiology), Clinical Nutrition & Dietetics, Home Science, Public Health, or BHMCT. Additionally, candidates with a BE/BTech in Food Technology from a recognized university    2. At least 50% aggregate marks in their undergraduate degree, demonstrating a solid academic foundation necessary for advanced studies in this challenging field                                     3. Minimum 60% in English in the qualifying exam. If not met, applicants must clear the Manipal Enablers English Competency Test and/or complete a 6-week Bridge Program with a minimum 60% pass grade. If the medium of instruction was not English, submit IELTS/TOEFL with an overall score of 6\n\nMBA in International Business: Applicants must have a Bachelor\'s Degree from a recognized university and must demonstrate proficiency in English. (Source: Master of Business Administration (MBA) Program) MSc in Applied Psychology: Prospective students should have a bachelor\'s degree of a minimum of three years in any discipline with at least 50% aggregate marks from a recognized university. (Source: Master of Science in Applied Psychology) MSc in Medical Biotechnology: Eligibility criteria require students to hold a bachelor\'s degree in any Life Science subject from a recognized university with at least 50% aggregate marks in their undergraduate degree. (Source: Msc in Medical Biotechnology) MSc in Information Science: Candidates should be a graduate with a BSc(IT)/BSc(ISM)/BCA/BSc (Computer Science)/B.Sc./BBA (IT)/B. Tech/B.E from a recognized University or any other graduate with a minimum of three years of experience in the field of IT. (Source: MSc Information Systems)\n\n1. BSc in Food and Nutrition Sciences, Allied Sciences (such as Medical, Agriculture, BHMS, BAMS), Life Sciences (including Botany, Zoology, Biotechnology, Microbiology), Clinical Nutrition & Dietetics, Home Science, Public Health, or BHMCT. Additionally, candidates with a BE/BTech in Food Technology from a recognized university 2. At least 50% aggregate marks in their undergraduate degree, demonstrating a solid academic foundation necessary for advanced studies in this challenging field 3. Minimum 60% in English in the qualifying exam. If not met, applicants must clear the Manipal Enablers English Competency Test and/or complete a 6-week Bridge Program with a minimum 60% pass grade. If the medium of instruction was not English, submit IELTS/TOEFL with an overall score of 6','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:50','2026-07-13 23:24:41',NULL);
INSERT INTO `courses` (`id`, `public_id`, `university_id`, `name`, `degree_level`, `duration_months`, `language`, `description`, `eligibility_criteria`, `status`, `created_by`, `created_at`, `updated_at`, `deleted_at`) VALUES (2531,'01KWJDMG0R06HSGY9K8RM8BBAX',145,'MSc - Information Science','bachelors',24,'English','Toolkit source: non_exclusive / UAE / row 70.','REQUIREMENTS / DOCUMENTS:\n1. BTech, BCA, BSc-IT, BSc-ISM, BSc-CS, BBA, or any other Undergraduate degree from a recognized institution/university\nA minimum of 50% marks in the qualifying degree and Completion of Mathematics, Statistics, or Information Systems as part of the undergraduate curriculum.                                        2. Minimum 60% in English in the qualifying exam. If not met, applicants must clear the Manipal Enablers English Competency Test and/or complete a 6-week Bridge Program with a minimum 60% pass grade. If the medium of instruction was not English, submit IELTS/TOEFL with an overall score of 6.                                        3. Lateral Entry (for Postgraduate Diploma Holders):\n\nStudents who have completed a Post Graduate Diploma in Data Science (PGDDS) or Post Graduate Diploma in Cyber Security (PGDCS) from the MAHE Dubai campus are eligible for admission into the second year of the MSc in Information Science program as a lateral entry.\n\nMBA in International Business: Applicants must have a Bachelor\'s Degree from a recognized university and must demonstrate proficiency in English. (Source: Master of Business Administration (MBA) Program) MSc in Applied Psychology: Prospective students should have a bachelor\'s degree of a minimum of three years in any discipline with at least 50% aggregate marks from a recognized university. (Source: Master of Science in Applied Psychology) MSc in Medical Biotechnology: Eligibility criteria require students to hold a bachelor\'s degree in any Life Science subject from a recognized university with at least 50% aggregate marks in their undergraduate degree. (Source: Msc in Medical Biotechnology) MSc in Information Science: Candidates should be a graduate with a BSc(IT)/BSc(ISM)/BCA/BSc (Computer Science)/B.Sc./BBA (IT)/B. Tech/B.E from a recognized University or any other graduate with a minimum of three years of experience in the field of IT. (Source: MSc Information Systems)\n\n1. BTech, BCA, BSc-IT, BSc-ISM, BSc-CS, BBA, or any other Undergraduate degree from a recognized institution/university A minimum of 50% marks in the qualifying degree and Completion of Mathematics, Statistics, or Information Systems as part of the undergraduate curriculum. 2. Minimum 60% in English in the qualifying exam. If not met, applicants must clear the Manipal Enablers English Competency Test and/or complete a 6-week Bridge Program with a minimum 60% pass grade. If the medium of instruction was not English, submit IELTS/TOEFL with an overall score of 6. 3. Lateral Entry (for Postgraduate Diploma Holders): Students who have completed a Post Graduate Diploma in Data Science (PGDDS) or Post Graduate Diploma in Cyber Security (PGDCS) from the MAHE Dubai campus are eligible for admission into the second year of the MSc in Information Science program as a lateral entry.','active',NULL,'2026-07-03 03:31:50','2026-07-13 23:24:41',NULL);
